<section class="wrap prose">
  <h2>Getting better at flags</h2>
  <p>Most flags are built from a small vocabulary of designs: vertical or horizontal tricolours, Nordic crosses, crescents and stars, and the Pan-African red, gold and green. Learning these "families" helps far more than memorising flags one by one. When two answers look plausible, check the order of the stripes — Ireland and Côte d'Ivoire use the same colours in mirror order, while Chad and Romania are almost identical. Flag images are served by flagcdn.com; each is a public-domain national symbol.</p>
  <p>Next, try <a href="capitals.html">Capital Quest</a> or look up any flag's country in the <a href="../atlas/index.html">world atlas</a>.</p>
</section>
